CORE
main.cpp
--unwind 5
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* elements copied while alive: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] .* list elements destroyed: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] .* each object destroyed once: SUCCESS$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The backing array of a std::initializer_list argument lives until the end
of the full-expression ([class.temporary]/4, [dcl.init.list]/6).  Its
elements were destroyed when the list object had been built, before the
callee read them, and those of a list of three or more elements twice.
